      "source": "hn",
      "title": "Show HN: Subvocal – Talk to your computer without making noise",
      "url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50340088",
      "author": "aarushyadav",
      "external_id": "50340088",
      "summary": null,
      "why_read": null,
      "authors": [],
      "category": null,
      "published": "2026-11-02T17:16:17Z",
      "score": 769,
      "comments": 359,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50340088",
      "snippet": "Hi HN, we&#x27;re Aarush and Arnav from The Subvocal Company (YC F26) (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;subvocal.company&#x2F;\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;subvocal.company&#x2F;</a>). We’re building smart glasses that let you talk to your computer without talking out loud. You can mouth words silently and discreetly and the glasses decode them to text at the speed of speech.<p>Here&#x27;s a video of Dave from YC trying it out: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.youtube.com&#x2F;watch?v=9QdX1eObVYI\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.youtube.com&#x2F;watch?v=9QdX1eObVYI</a><p>(Edit: you don&#x27;t actually have to move your lips or even open your mouth for this to work! Since the RF can see inside your mouth the system can be fine tuned on &quot;internal speech&quot;. This isn&#x27;t the automatic tongue movements that occur when &quot;thinking&quot; words to yourself, but more like mouthing with your lip",
      "links": []
    },
