      "source": "hn",
      "title": "Show HN: Warsaw in voxels – An interactive 3D map of the city centre",
      "url": "https://p.migdal.pl/warsaw-vibe-voxel/",
      "author": "stared",
      "external_id": "50339221",
      "summary": null,
      "why_read": null,
      "authors": [],
      "category": null,
      "published": "2026-11-02T16:25:26Z",
      "score": 304,
      "comments": 50,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50339221",
      "snippet": "Explore central Warsaw in voxels - slightly inspired by Minecraft, and MagicaVoxel. \nYou can change the date, time of day and weather, explore the city, or click on a pedestrian to control them (here a bit of inspiration from Dungeon Keeper).<p>Works best on desktop, but I tried to make it usable on mobile too. The initial load can take a while. It&#x27;s based on several open datasets, including:<p>- OpenStreetMap (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.openstreetmap.org&#x2F;#map=6&#x2F;52.02&#x2F;19.14\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.openstreetmap.org&#x2F;#map=6&#x2F;52.02&#x2F;19.14</a>) - buildings, streets, sidewalks, tram tracks, etc<p>- GUGiK &#x2F; Geoportal (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.geoportal.gov.pl&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.geoportal.gov.pl&#x2F;</a>) - LiDAR for building heights and trees, aerial imagery for colours<p>- Warsaw&#x27;s city tree database ",
      "links": []
    },
