    {
      "source": "hn",
      "title": "Launch HN: Momentic (YC W24) – Agents that catch bugs by using your app",
      "url": "https://momentic.ai/",
      "author": "wuweiweiwu",
      "external_id": "50339913",
      "summary": null,
      "why_read": null,
      "authors": [],
      "category": null,
      "published": "2026-11-02T17:05:25Z",
      "score": 155,
      "comments": 103,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50339913",
      "snippet": "Hey HN, we’re Wei-Wei and Jeff. We’re building Momentic, QA agents that autonomously plan, explore, and bug-bash controls and user flows in your web, iOS, Android, and (soon) desktop apps to catch bugs.<p>Here’s a demo: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;youtu.be&#x2F;BFsM-Se1Fh8\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;youtu.be&#x2F;BFsM-Se1Fh8</a><p>We’re both software engineers that spent our careers on dev tooling and infra across companies like Robinhood, Retool, WeWork, and Qualtrics. Testing was always a pain in the ass (esp Playwright and Selenium), so we built agents to do it for us.<p>Modern day software has a ton of bugs and the change failure rate is only growing faster as coding agent adoption scales. LLMs are really good at generating code, but reinforce their own assumptions, write a ton of useless tests, and are bad at visual understanding. On DeepSWE v1.1, Sonnet 5.5 hit 66.2% pass rat",
      "links": []
    },
